IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cidra-types`
IMPORT `cidra-misrepresentation`
IMPORT `cidra-remedies`
IMPORT `cidra-goal`

-- Consumer Insurance (Disclosure and Representations) Act 2012 (UK) — the
-- encoder's tests. Expected values are worked by hand from the Act.

§ `Tests`

consumer MEANS `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
lifeCover MEANS `Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

-- Fields: made, reasonable care, dishonest, knew untrue, reasonable consumer
-- would know untrue, knew relevant, reasonable consumer would know relevant,
-- clear question.
careless MEANS `Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST FALSE, FALSE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
reasonable MEANS `Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, JUST FALSE, FALSE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
deliberate MEANS `Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

-- Premium charged £250, paid £250; £40 unfair to retain; claim £10,000, or
-- £8,000 under the different terms.
money MEANS `Money facts` OF 250, 250, 40, 10000, 8000

GIVEN different IS A BOOLEAN, higher IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What the insurer would have done`
`would have contracted, different terms` different `, premium` higher MEANS
    `the contract, on these terms` different higher

§§ `Goal 1 — does the Act apply`

#ASSERT `the Act applies to` consumer
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`Contract facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`Contract facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the Act applies to` (`Contract facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE))

§§ `Goal 2 — qualifying misrepresentations and their class`

-- s 4(1)(a): reasonable care taken, no remedy; s 3(5) dishonesty is never
-- reasonable care.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` reasonable `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money)
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` (`Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money
-- s 4(1)(b): inducement.
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` careless `given` `the same contract on the same terms` `and` money)
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` careless `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` TRUE `, premium` 250) `and` money
#ASSERT `is a qualifying misrepresentation` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` FALSE `, premium` 500) `and` money
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` FALSE `, premium` 250) `and` money)
#ASSERT NOT (`is a qualifying misrepresentation` (`Misrepresentation facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST FALSE, FALSE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money)

-- s 5(2): both limbs needed.
#ASSERT `the class of` deliberate EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`
#ASSERT `the class of` careless EQUALS `careless`
#ASSERT `the class of` (`Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST TRUE, TRUE, JUST FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS `careless`
-- s 5(5)(a): nothing shown, a reasonable consumer would have known it
-- untrue; (b) a clear and specific question: presumed deliberate or reckless.
#ASSERT `the class of` (`Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS `deliberate or reckless`
-- No clear question, and a reasonable consumer would not have known it
-- relevant: careless.
#ASSERT `the class of` (`Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, NOTHING, TRUE, NOTHING, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS `careless`
-- The contrary shown displaces the presumption.
#ASSERT `the class of` (`Misrepresentation facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, JUST FALSE, TRUE, NOTHING, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS `careless`

§§ `Goal 3 — remedies`

-- Para 2: deliberate or reckless — avoid; keep premiums except £40.
r1 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` deliberate `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money
#ASSERT r1's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT r1's `premiums to return` EQUALS 40
#ASSERT r1's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0

-- Para 5: careless, no contract at all — avoid, return all £250.
r2 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` careless `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money
#ASSERT r2's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`
#ASSERT r2's `premiums to return` EQUALS 250
#ASSERT r2's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 0

-- Paras 7-8: a premium of £500, not £250 — X = 50%, £5,000.
r3 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` FALSE `, premium` 500) `and` money
#ASSERT NOT (r3's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`)
#ASSERT r3's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT NOT (r3's `contract treated as on the different terms`)
#ASSERT r3's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
#ASSERT r3's `may terminate by reasonable notice`

-- Para 6 with 7: different terms (£8,000) and a premium of £400: X = 62.5%,
-- £5,000.
r4 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` TRUE `, premium` 400) `and` money
#ASSERT r4's `contract treated as on the different terms`
#ASSERT r4's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 5000
-- Para 6 alone: £8,000.
r5 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` TRUE `, premium` 250) `and` money
#ASSERT r5's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 8000
-- Para 9(5): no termination of life insurance; notice still possible.
r6 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` lifeCover `and` careless `given` (`would have contracted, different terms` FALSE `, premium` 500) `and` money
#ASSERT NOT (r6's `may terminate by reasonable notice`)
#ASSERT r6's `may give notice of its rights for the future`
-- No qualifying misrepresentation: paid in full.
r7 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` reasonable `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` money
#ASSERT r7's `amount payable on the claim` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT NOT (r7's `may avoid the contract and refuse all claims`)

§§ `The top-level goal`

pos MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`Misrepresentation case` OF consumer, careless, `would have contracted, different terms` FALSE `, premium` 500, money)
#ASSERT pos's `the Act applies`
#ASSERT pos's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT pos's `class` EQUALS JUST `careless`
business MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`Misrepresentation case` OF (`Contract facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE), careless, `no contract on any terms`, money)
#ASSERT NOT (business's `the Act applies`)
#ASSERT business's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS NOTHING
noQual MEANS `the misrepresentation position for` (`Misrepresentation case` OF consumer, reasonable, `no contract on any terms`, money)
#ASSERT noQual's `qualifying misrepresentation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT noQual's `class` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Added after the independent pass`

-- Para 9(6): after the insurer's notice the consumer may terminate, even for
-- life insurance.
#ASSERT r6's `consumer may terminate after the insurer's notice`
#ASSERT r3's `consumer may terminate after the insurer's notice`
#ASSERT NOT (r2's `consumer may terminate after the insurer's notice`)
-- Para 2(b): what is returned is never more than the premiums paid.
r8 MEANS `the insurer's remedy for` consumer `and` deliberate `given` `no contract on any terms` `and` (`Money facts` OF 250, 100, 400, 10000, 8000)
#ASSERT r8's `premiums to return` EQUALS 100
